---
// Privacy policy for the personal tools that run under rainforest.tools, including the Google
// OAuth app ("Hermes") in the rainforest-homelab Google Cloud project. Google requires a public
// privacy policy URL on an authorized domain before an External app can leave Testing mode.
export const prerender = true;

import Layout from '@layouts/index.astro';

const updated = '2026-11-23';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy">
  <main class="container flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-6 py-10 leading-relaxed">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm opacity-70">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p>
      This policy covers the personal tools Rainforest Cheng runs under
      rainforest.tools, including the Google OAuth app named "Hermes". These
      tools are built for personal and household use. They are not a commercial
      service and are not offered to the public.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">What data is accessed</h2>
    <p>
      When you sign in with Google and grant access, the app can read and, where
      you allow it, write the Google data covered by the scopes you approved,
      such as Google Calendar events and Google Drive files. It uses that data
      only to carry out what you ask for, for example listing today's events or
      saving a file you asked to save.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">How it is stored</h2>
    <p>
      OAuth tokens and any data the app works with are kept on a computer the
      owner controls. Nothing is sold, used for advertising, or shared with
      third parties, except the AI model provider that processes a request when
      you ask the assistant to act on your data.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Google API Services</h2>
    <p>
      The app's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs
      adheres to the
      <a
        class="underline"
        href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
        >Google API Services User Data Policy</a
      >, including the Limited Use requirements.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Revoking access</h2>
    <p>
      You can remove the app's access at any time at
      <a class="underline" href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions"
        >myaccount.google.com/permissions</a
      >. Tokens stored for you are deleted on request.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy can be sent through the
      <a class="underline" href="/#contact-form-footer">contact form</a> on the home
      page.
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>
